|notes=The 2006 slip uses the singular ‘a card’ for the Chewie or Wookiee take during your turn. The [[Chewbacca (V) (Virtual Set 3: Revolution) (Original)|original-edition slip]] survives in the consolidated PDF made in February 2003. The sheet gives 20 September 2002 as the set’s tournament-legality date, and the complete set was available by 21 September. The [[Chewbacca (V) (Virtual Set 3: Revolution) (Remastered 2006)|2006 publication]] gives its text as of 4 December 2006. [https://web.archive.org/web/20090816063441id_/http://www.starwarsccg.org/Resources/AR/AR1.7.1.pdf#page=21 Period One Rule, p. 21].
|sources=* [https://res.starwarsccg.org/legacyblocks/VirtualCards3.pdf#page=1 VirtualCards3.pdf] — the Players Committee's Virtual Set #3 sheet (PDF made 3 February 2003, a February 2003 re-issue; legal date on the sheet 20 September 2002; first release date unknown); page 1, slip 4. Slip image and game text from this sheet. Preserved copy: [https://web.archive.org/web/20261008193702/https://res.starwarsccg.org/legacyblocks/VirtualCards3.pdf Internet Archive primary-source copy].
* Lore and art: the printed Decipher card, [[Chewbacca]].
* 2006 publication: [[Chewbacca (V) (Virtual Set 3: Revolution) (Remastered 2006)]] (the 4 December 2006 remaster).
|hatnote=Other versions of this Virtual Original card: [[Chewbacca (V) (Virtual Set 3: Revolution) (Remastered 2006)]]. For the Decipher card this slip modifies, see [[Chewbacca]].
